  "generated_text": "1. **Identify the sides of the triangle and the vertex angle:**\n   The sides of the triangle are $\\cos x,$ $\\cos x,$ and $\\cos 7x,$ and the vertex angle is $2x.$\n\n2. **Apply the Law of Cosines:**\n   By the Law of Cosines, we have:\n   \\[\n   (\\cos 7x)^2 = (\\cos x)^2 + (\\cos x)^2 - 2(\\cos x)(\\cos x)(\\cos 2x).\n   \\]\n   Simplifying, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\cos^2 7x = 2 \\cos^2 x - 2 \\cos^2 x \\cos 2x.\n   \\]\n\n3. **Simplify the equation:**\n   Using the identity $\\cos 2x = 2 \\cos^2 x - 1,$ we can rewrite the equation as:\n   \\[\n   \\cos^2 7x = 2 \\cos^2 x - 2 \\cos^2 x (2 \\cos^2 x - 1).\n   \\]\n   Simplifying further, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\cos^2 7x = ",
